{
  "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
  "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard D. Friedman)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court can decide these cases, as it decided Crawford without testing the outer bounds of the Confrontation Clause, by adopting a simple proposition that is easily understood by and intuitively sensible to ordinary lay people and so capable of being passed on from generation to generation as one of the cornerstones of our fundamental liberties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When, for example, there's an undercover agent, a law enforcement officer -- let's think of the mafia or the Ku Klux Klan reveals himself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard D. Friedman)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's a continuing conspiracy, but -- but that statement to the law enforcement officer saying that somebody else in the conspiracy has committed a crime, would not, in fact, be in furtherance of the conspiracy. It would blow the conspiracy apart."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if a statement is made to a known law enforcement officer providing information that's -- that's very incriminating against somebody, but it doesn't specifically identify that person? Does that fall within your test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard D. Friedman)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe -- I believe so. Now -- now, in fact, that would provide some identifying information because it is a person who is associated with that blue -- with that blue Toyota."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard D. Friedman)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California and Oregon have already adopted such statutes, and -- and my State of Michigan is on the verge of doing so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard D. Friedman)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I actually testified last month before the Michigan House on the -- the bill saying I believe this bill is blatantly unconstitutional. I believe it's going to be held unconstitutional within a few months."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's -- what's worrying me on this is -- I'll tell you my concern without the hypothetical. Crawford wrenches the Confrontation Clause free of the hearsay rule, and therefore, testimony -- it might be testimonial even though it is not hearsay or falls within an -- doesn't fall within an exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard D. Friedman)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not propose that this categorical principle that an accusation to a law enforcement officer is a definition of what's testimonial. We regard this as a core category of testimonial statements such as the core categories that the Court listed in Crawford."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Edmund Burke say that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Isn't -- isn't the problem, though -- I mean, as Crawford said, those examples defined the core."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So what's the test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Which were?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Well, which were in particular, we know, affidavits. We also know something about letters, and the question with the tape recording is, is it enough like, does it resemble those enough?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: There was no such effort, Your Honor. But, well, here, if I may be permitted to go beyond the record just a little bit, what we -- what we do know is that the case was continued one time because Amy Hammon did not show up in response to a subpoena, and that the second time, the -- the trial proceeded. But there was no effort to send someone out to -- to enforce it or to bring any sort of contempt sanction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: The affidavit is not admissible."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: He's -- he's still a --\nJUSTICE STEVENS: He's still the witness\nwe're concerned about.\nMR. GORNSTEIN: He is the witness --\nJUSTICE STEVENS: Therefore, he's subject to\ncross examination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: No. I -- I think that what\nyou would look to see is if, at the relevant time, that\n-- that the declarant was acting as a witness. And at\nthe relevant time, when somebody is answering a\nquestion to avert an immediate danger, they're not\nacting as a witness. They're not making a solemn\ndeclaration for the purpose of proving facts to support\na prosecution, and so they're not acting as a witness\nin those circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But under your test, the whole question is whether the emergency continued at the time the witness' words are being repeated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5705",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3192486417bd087e8993a3e0a92d682b2f65128073bd60b594d87cbed14dc5ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192486417bd-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
